WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
- So let's start with Diamond.

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.230
What's going on with you girl?

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.720
- Yes, well, Kelly, I'll be honest.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.330
I've always been a super confident woman.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.610
Like, I'm the life of the
party when I step into a room,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.430
I am bringing so much positive energy.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.350
I'm a mom,

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.410
I have my own business doing
social media management.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.280
I host events.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.770
And so with this year and
everything that's going on,

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.390
it literally stopped, as we all know,

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:28.350
and it totally knocked me off my square.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.290
Everything paused, and I was really left

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.710
feeling lost and angry

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.620
and just really not knowing what to do.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.470
I lost a lot of
connections with the people

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.213
and I really thrive off
that human connection.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.540
Just tryna figure out how to
pivot my business in this time

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.030
where it's like so many
events and getting out there.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:47.870
So I need to figure out

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:50.310
how do I get that confidence back, right?

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.390
Find that confident strong woman

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.630
that I know deep down inside that I am.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.010
So I can really continue
to inspire my children,

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:57.843
my daughters.

00:00:57.843 --> 00:00:58.850
And so I'm just tryna figure out like,

00:00:58.850 --> 00:00:59.990
where do I even begin

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:03.260
with the year being so crazy and draining?

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.270
- I, well, maybe with
that meditation thing

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.930
he was just talking about,
but let's talk to Dr. Chopra.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:11.240
- One thing you can do instinctly
anytime you're stressed

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:15.700
is use what I call the STOP formula.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.890
S-T-O-P.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.350
S stands for stop,

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.110
T stands for take three deep breaths

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:27.150
and smile from your head
to your toes, everywhere.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.680
O, observe your breath and
your body, the sensations.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.930
And then P, proceed with
awareness, compassion, and joy.

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:37.950
But what you're also doing,
which is very effective,

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.150
is you're expressing your vulnerability.

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.530
And that is very important.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:42.920
It's a sign of strength

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.850
when we express our
vulnerabilities to each other,

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:46.690
we are stronger.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:49.910
So we ask for help, and we give help.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:51.260
Social scientists there days

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.880
talk about something called
the happiness formula,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.040
which is basically,

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.530
are you seeing problems or
are you seeing opportunities?

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.290
What are the conditions of your living?

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:02.080
And do you have meaning and purpose?

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.290
And can you make other people happy?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.380
The fastest way to increase
your self esteem and be happy

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.300
is to make somebody else happy.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.840
- That, I, that's my favorite
thing that I've kind of

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.860
heard people say in this time,

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.470
'cause doing this show it's been

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:18.550
absolutely a blessing for me
personally because you hear,

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.770
you hear people say, "You know,

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.060
if you're having a hard time

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.650
why don't you help someone else?"

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.090
Not only does it just kinda take you away

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.520
from your own egocentric
moment that you're suffering,

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.367
but you're focusing on
someone else you're helping

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:29.100
and so and that makes you feel good.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.520
And it's so true.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.960
Do you ever, do you feel like that?

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.390
- Absolutely, I spend a
lot of my time doing that

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.920
to make myself feel better

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.750
when I can't just make myself feel better.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.640
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- You know, I find that

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.490
if you're able to help someone bridge

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:45.440
that gap of trying to get
to that spot, whether it's,

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.740
you know, just to having a
conversation or being able to,

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.360
you know, help with this month's rent, or

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.353
it's something as small as
just being an ear to listen to.

